{"data": [{"author_id": "1161370756208648193", "created_at": "2026-11-09T20:52:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119895814676091118"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 137, "start": 128, "tag": "FEDSNote"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/…", "end": 175, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/gold-reserve-relocations-are-they-always-bad-news-for-u-s-dollar-reserves-20261109.html", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119895816576057344/NQ8ciK3y?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119895816576057344/NQ8ciK3y?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 152, "status": 200, "title": "Gold Reserve Relocations: Are They Always Bad News for U.S. Dollar Reserves?", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/gold-reserve-relocations-are-they-always-bad-news-for-u-s-dollar-reserves-20261109.html", "url": "https://t.co/lHagPzocUu"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/yetGyDypAB", "end": 199, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2119895814676091118/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119895708853497856", "start": 176, "url": "https://t.co/yetGyDypAB"}]}, "id": "2119895814676091118", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 140, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What happened to the US dollar share of Euro Area central banks' FX reserves when they moved gold reserves out of the US? A new #FEDSNote investigates. https://t.co/lHagPzocUu https://t.co/yetGyDypAB", "url": "https://x.com/FedResearch/status/2119895814676091118"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-09T20:47:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119894795128885606"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/nicktimiraos/s…", "end": 44, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/nicktimiraos/status/2119885620676043121", "start": 21, "url": "https://t.co/fxgg80Axay"}]}, "id": "2119894795128885606", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1332, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119885620676043121", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Econvitals makes it! https://t.co/fxgg80Axay", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2119894795128885606"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-11-09T20:16:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119886832934801839"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/claudeai/statu…", "end": 49, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/claudeai/status/2119867114450268322", "start": 26, "url": "https://t.co/XH8Bk7XXPw"}]}, "id": "2119886832934801839", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1338, "like_count": 28, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119867114450268322", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Update all the way, folks https://t.co/XH8Bk7XXPw", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2119886832934801839"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-11-09T20:11:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119885620676043121"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/CFM7ikw8fO", "end": 286, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2119885620676043121/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119885222653087744", "start": 263, "url": "https://t.co/CFM7ikw8fO"}]}, "id": "2119885620676043121", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 23, "impression_count": 23243, "like_count": 81, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "Economists expect growth in the core CPI to have moderated in October to around 0.22%, though the full range of estimates is broad enough to round down to 0.1% or round up to 0.3%.\n\nDue to the government shutdown in Oct 2025, there's no tidy year-earlier figure. https://t.co/CFM7ikw8fO", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2119885620676043121"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:50:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119880222569075055"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "So far the AI economy is less a story about data centers than about the stock market—and that is also where the risk is.", "display_url": "econvitals.org/posts/2026-11-…", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://econvitals.org/posts/2026-11-09-ai-boom-two-engines/", "images": [{"height": 1517, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119851867546988544/nD-QqZuX?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1520}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119851867546988544/nD-QqZuX?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 232, "status": 200, "title": "The AI Boom’s Two Engines", "unwound_url": "https://econvitals.org/posts/2026-11-09-ai-boom-two-engines/", "url": "https://t.co/jKTsluerUp"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/wjlvXK2RGs", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2119880222569075055/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119878623209373696", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/wjlvXK2RGs"}]}, "id": "2119880222569075055", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 16, "impression_count": 5039, "like_count": 34, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "New piece on the economics of the AI buildout based on running it through the Fed's FRB/US model.\n\nShort version: The stock market increase has been an even bigger deal than the actual infrastructure build.\n\nWill share more later.\n\nhttps://t.co/jKTsluerUp https://t.co/wjlvXK2RGs", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2119880222569075055"}, {"author_id": "15072071", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:49:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119880062862299514"], "id": "2119880062862299514", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1217, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "The 12th U.S. Treasury Market Conference, held in September, focused on how to maintain smooth functioning in the Treasury market amid ongoing structural changes. Today's post highlights the three central themes that emerged at the conference: modernization, innovation, and", "url": "https://x.com/NewYorkFed/status/2119880062862299514"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:35:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119876449494540554"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Be the villain of a Saturday-morning mystery cartoon. Scare everyone out of Grimsby Manor before those meddling kids unmask you.", "display_url": "…-have-gotten-away-with-it.netlify.app", "end": 278, "expanded_url": "https://i-would-have-gotten-away-with-it.netlify.app/", "start": 255, "status": 200, "title": "I Would Have Gotten Away With It", "unwound_url": "https://i-would-have-gotten-away-with-it.netlify.app/", "url": "https://t.co/5nnkYI6bV6"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/hBTWJUQ0F3", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2119876449494540554/video/1", "media_key": "13_2119876130807197696", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/hBTWJUQ0F3"}]}, "id": "2119876449494540554", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 60, "impression_count": 11964, "like_count": 173, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 31, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "In addition to more serious examples I shared in my post, I had Fable 5.2 build a parody reverse Scooby Doo game where you have to scare away meddling kids. Here is the trailer it made (including the music and sounds) and the game (which is fun) is here: https://t.co/5nnkYI6bV6 https://t.co/hBTWJUQ0F3", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2119876449494540554"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:19:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119872524326420490"], "id": "2119872524326420490", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 13624, "like_count": 32, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "For the sake of both current and future generations, the UK's economic debate needs to move boldly beyond simple budget arithmetic. As such, it is encouraging to see a comprehensive growth strategy coming together.\nNeedless to say, sustained implementation will be key.", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119872524326420490"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:10:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119870150845599972"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "General, often expert, and sometimes jagged", "display_url": "oneusefulthing.org/p/fable-52-and…", "end": 291, "expanded_url": "https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/fable-52-and-jagged-agi", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119870157875200000/vOiJHlqz?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119870157875200000/vOiJHlqz?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 268, "status": 200, "title": "Fable 5.2 and Jagged AGI", "unwound_url": "https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/fable-52-and-jagged-agi", "url": "https://t.co/QiR0IFPrZY"}]}, "id": "2119870150845599972", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 610, "impression_count": 60651, "like_count": 1206, "quote_count": 30, "reply_count": 101, "retweet_count": 91}, "text": "I had early access to Fable 5.2 for a bit &amp; I think  it crosses the line into being a sort of Jagged AGI. Here, I have it launch a business, do academic research, hack hardware, build 3D models &amp; more. I think it is a good illustration of limits &amp; powers: https://t.co/QiR0IFPrZY", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2119870150845599972"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-09T18:59:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119867372664434754"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 127, "id": "26579339", "start": 122, "username": "PIIE"}, {"end": 134, "id": "25390350", "start": 129, "username": "OECD"}, {"end": 156, "id": "27860681", "start": 141, "username": "WorldBankGroup"}], "urls": [